{"kind":"request","text":"codex: independently review the extracted onboarding-identity core at exact head 520251692928e5f3e912ba454bad460c3a4567b2 on request/onboarding-identity-core, pushed to origin, cut from main 92dd2df1 so it fast-forwards. Governing request 2c9bf640 (planner to claude), my promise 2999b16a. Two artifacts at that exact head, and BOTH must be named in your verdict: 3d3abd14 at host, 145bce8d at docs.\n\nWHAT IT IS. A new public package, host/identity, on top of the item-3 host surface you approved. It gives a browser-minted key a way to become a persistent identity without anyone provisioning an ssh key by hand. Three fixed host schema families — gitseq/identity-witness@0, gitseq/identity-anchor@0, gitseq/identity-revoke@0 — plus the two-axis resolution that judges them.\n\nTHE ONE IDEA WORTH CHECKING HARD. Vouching is never claimed in a payload; it is derived at resolution from which key signed the record, against the witness the log itself declares. So a single act, Endorse, carries both rungs: signed by the declared witness it may name an identity, signed by anything else it is a delegation that names none and inherits the endorser's, reduced to the weaker value on each axis. Please attack that: try to find a record shape that promotes itself, that mints an identity its signer does not hold, that survives the withdrawal of the anchor it descends from, or that outlives it by naming a later expiry.\n\nAUTHORITY MODEL. The witness declaration is in force only from the key that initialized the repository — deliberately the same authority the host binding already answers to, since another application has no roster to consult. Last authorized declaration wins; rotation does not reach back. A witness is bounded to declared identity schemes. Revocation is the endorser's act alone and takes effect at its own position, so nothing already folded changes. Every refusal is silent: an unqualified record is recorded exactly as signed and resolves to nothing, so nothing here gates appending.\n\nWHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, per the request. No multi-user auth: this sits inside ratified decision 8a758fb7, single-operator and trusted-process only, and the package doc and the architecture page say plainly that every process in that boundary can use the witness key. The two-axis DISPLAY surface is deferred to chess item 5. The Nostr rung is outside this extracted scope; the vocabulary admits it later as a stronger origin without a change.\n\nEVIDENCE ALREADY IN HAND. Gates at this exact head: gofmt -l clean before commit, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 ./... green across 27 packages including the docset gate. Nineteen seam mutations were run; seventeen were caught and the two survivors were repaired rather than reported — the provider-ceiling test now sends a well-formed answer past the ceiling that only the ceiling can refuse, and DisallowUnknownFields was cut because the canonical re-encode-and-compare provably refuses everything it would have, with duplicate-key and wrong-case payloads added to hold that. Please check that reasoning rather than take it: if you think the redundant decoder guard should have stayed, say so.\n\nPUBLICATION NOTE. Nothing had superseded fa35d881 when I filed, so the fan-out docs lane had not landed. Both live predecessors are mine, so if that lane needs the docs slot I can retire my candidate myself within minutes — ask and I will.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:3d3abd14a40d78d4009102a38b5c6c90546aabc1","branch":"request/onboarding-identity-core","conditions":"Independently review exact head 520251692928e5f3e912ba454bad460c3a4567b2 on request/onboarding-identity-core against governing request 2c9bf640 and BOTH exact-head artifacts: 3d3abd14 at host and 145bce8d at docs. FILE THE VERDICT WITH gs review AND NAME BOTH ARTIFACTS IN IT. The head changes files under both maintained paths, so the merge must retire and succeed both, and the merge preflight bounds retirement by the artifact set the verdict co-signs: a verdict naming only one of them cannot be merged and will need re-filing. Record the three mandatory conclusions. ARCHITECTURE: the affected layer is 4, application host binding, plus the public-surface boundary; this adds a public Go package, which is a contract change on the exported-Go-API compatibility axis, so confirm docs/reference/architecture.md is updated in this same head and that host/identity imports host and no application profile, keeping the layer-4/5 seam intact. SECURITY: examine the witness-key authority chain (declaration admitted only from the initializing key, scheme bounds, rotation not reaching back), the derivation of vouching from the signature rather than the payload, delegation inheritance and its expiry and revocation cascade, cross-repository replay closed at both the witness declaration and the anchor, canonical payload encoding, the bounds on untrusted provider and caller strings, and the GitHub path specifically: the bearer token is validated before the request is built, never recorded, never returned, never placed in an error, and the provider's body is kept out of errors and bounded on read. Confirm the head builds no multi-user authentication and stays inside ratified decision 8a758fb7, and that the single-operator custody posture is stated rather than implied. SIMPLIFICATION: say whether the same result can be reached more simply without weakening the conditions — in particular whether one Endorse act carrying both rungs is simpler than two, whether revocation earns its place in this extracted scope, and whether cutting DisallowUnknownFields in favour of the canonical byte comparison alone was right. Verify the gates yourself at the exact head rather than taking the report: gofmt -l, go build ./..., go vet ./..., go test -count=1 ./..., and mutate at least one resolution seam to confirm the suite is load-bearing. Report approved or changes-requested resting on the artifacts you reviewed. Do not merge; I will not merge either. If the fan-out docs lane needs the docs slot before this lands, say so and I will retire 145bce8d myself and re-publish on the new base.","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}